{
  "title": "Leg Length Discrepancy (LLD)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4045/leg-length-discrepancy-lld",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 31 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Leg Length Discrepancy is a common condition that may be caused by a congenital defect, disruption of the physis, or a paralytic disorder and presents with limb length asymmetry of varying magnitude.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with block testing and radiographic scanography. CT studies can be used to calculate LLD in the presence of contractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation with or without shoe lifts for differences < 2 cm at skeletal maturity. Surgical intervention is indicated for differences > 2 cm, with different techniques depending on the discrepancy magnitude and remaining skeletal growth.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "2cm LLD occurs in up to 2/3 of the population",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Common causes of LLD",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**congenital disorders**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hemihypertrophy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "dysplasias",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "PFFD",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "DDH",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "unilateral clubfoot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**paralytic disorders**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "spasticity (cerebral palsy)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "polio",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**physis disruption**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tumor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**back pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increased prevalence of **back pain**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**osteoarthritis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreased coverage of femoral head on long leg side leads to **osteoarthritis** 84% of the time",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**functional scoliosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inefficient gait",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "equinus contracture of ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Static",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "malunion of femur or tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Progressive",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "physeal growth arrest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "congenital",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "absolute discrepancy increases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "proportion stats the same",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**block testing**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "with the patient standing, add blocks under the short leg until the pelvis is level, then measure the blocks to determine the discrepancy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "block testing is considered the best initial screening method",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**tape measurement**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "measure from the anterior superior iliac spine to the medial malleolus with a tape measure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "evaluate for hip, knee and ankle **contractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "affect apparent limb length",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hip adduction contracture causes apparent shortening of adducted side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**teleoroentgenography (scanography)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4045/images/leg%20lenght%20discrepancy%20scanogram_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "measure discrepancy with single exposure from 2m away",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**bone age hand films**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "determine bone age with bone age xray (hand)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT Scanography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "CT scanography is the **most accurate diagnostic test with contractures of the hip, knee, or ankle**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLD Projections",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "General assumptions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "growth continues until **16 yrs in boys** and until **14 yrs in girls**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Methods to project LLD at maturity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Mosley graph",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "estimation technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leg grows **23 mm/year**, with most of that coming from the knee (**15 mm/yr**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "proximal femur - 3 mm / yr (1/8 in)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "distal femur - 9 mm / yr (3/8 in)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "proximal tibia - 6 mm / yr (1/4 in)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "distal tibia - 5 mm / yr (3/16 in)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Can be tracked with",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Green-Anderson tables",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4045/images/ga%20chart.jpg",
                  "caption": "Green and Anderson chart"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4045/images/leg%20lenght%20discrepancy%20scanogram_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "uses extremity length for a given age",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Moseley straight line graph",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "improves on Green-Anderson method by reformatting data in a graph form",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "accounts for differences between skeletal and chronologic age",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "minimizes error",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "averages serial measurements",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Multiplier method",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prediction based on multiplying the current discrepancy by a sex and age specific factor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "most accurate for congenital LLD",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "1/2 of final leg length",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "girls at age 3",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "boys at age 4",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "shoe lift or **observation only**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**< 2 cm** projected LLD at maturity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "not associated with scoliosis or back pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "shortening of long side via epiphysiodesis of femur, tibia, or both",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**2-5 cm** projected LLD",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "limb lengthening of short side",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**> 5 cm** projected LLD",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lengthening often combined with a shortening procedure (epiphysiodesis, ostectomy) on long side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "physeal bar excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bony bridge involves <50% of physis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "at least 2 years left of growth",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "amputation and prosthetic fitting",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "non-reconstructable limb",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**> 20 cm**projected LLD",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Distraction osteogenesis** (Ilizarov principles)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "initiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "perform osteotomy and place fixator",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "metaphyseal corticotomy to preserve medullary canal and blood supply",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "success with modern techniques utilizing intramedullary implants suggests that preservation of periosteal blood supply is more important than endosteal blood supply",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "distraction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "wait 5-7 days then begin distraction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "distract **~ 1 mm/day**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "following distraction keep fixator on for as many days as you lengthened",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "concurrent procedures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may lengthen over a nail so ex-fix can be removed sooner",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lengthening often combined with a shortening procedure (epiphysiodesis, ostectomy) on long side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Incomplete arrest/ angular deformity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "percutaneous technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Pin site infections**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Fracture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Delayed union**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Premature cessation of lengthening**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Persistent limb length discrepancy due to error in timing of surgery**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Joint subluxation/dislocation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Mechanical axis deviation (MAD)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lengthening along the anatomical axis of the femur leads to lateral MAD",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "shortening along the anatomical axis of the femur leads to medial MAD",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
